    "thesis": "A Caribbean belvedere estate organized as a ceremonial arrival plinth, a broad ocean-facing social salon, a lower guest wing, and a more secluded elevated family-and-owner pavilion. Deep limestone terraces frame the sea-facing edge while warm timber, ivory render, bronze openings, and sage-toned screened service volumes give the composition a refined tropical character without relying on ornamental facade detail.",
